iio-sensor-proxy-ssc (3.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 built with
    -Dssc-support=enabled, so the sensors that Qualcomm's Sensor Core serves
    through libssc (ambient light and compass by default, accelerometer and
    proximity through udev rules) are exported on D-Bus as
    net.hadess.SensorProxy together with the plain IIO sensors.
  * Named iio-sensor-proxy-ssc and declared as the SSC-capable replacement for
    iio-sensor-proxy: Provides/Replaces/Conflicts, following
    sheng_fedora_packages/iio-sensor-proxy-ssc.spec. The archive package is
    built without SSC support because libssc is not in Debian or Ubuntu, so
    both cannot usefully be installed together.
  * Nothing else is changed from upstream 3.9: the D-Bus name, the unit name
    and the file layout are stock, which keeps marble-device-support's
    iio-sensor-proxy.service drop-in and the rootfs enable list valid.
  * Built with -Dudevrulesdir/-Dsystemdsystemunitdir so configure needs
    neither udev.pc nor systemd.pc from the build container.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:28:00 +0800
